## Why This Is Asked
Assesses practical PIM/JIT implementation with governance.

## Key Concepts
- Privileged Identity Management (PIM)
- Just-In-Time (JIT) access
- Activation workflow and MFA
- Approvals, auditing, and alerts
- Emergency break-glass handling

## Code Example
```javascript
// PIM-like activation flow (illustrative)
const activate = async (roleId, user) => {
  // request activation with approval
  await graphClient.post(`/roleAssignments`, { roleDefinitionId: roleId, principalId: user });
  // MFA enforcement occurs at login/activation
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the emergency bypass path and ensure controls aren’t bypassed?
- How would you export and present an audit report of activations for compliance?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests cross-tenant governance, external collaboration, and how to enforce least privilege with scalable delegation. It also probes how to combine Lighthouse, B2B, PIM, CA, and auditing for a measurable, auditable workflow.

## Key Concepts

- Azure Lighthouse delegation model across tenants
- B2B collaboration and identity management
- Granular RBAC scoping (subscription, resource group, resource)
- Time-bound access with PIM or entitlement packages
- Conditional Access and MFA enforcement
- Auditing, monitoring, and threat detection (Azure Activity Logs, Sentinel)
- Sandbox testing and rollback strategies

